; A stack group's saved accumulator holding a DTP-BODY-FORWARD is restored as
; saved and left alone by the scavenger (sys/ucadr/uc-stack-groups.lisp
; SG-LOAD-BLOCK-INTO-PDL-BUFFER, uc-storage-allocation.lisp SCAVL3).  Load
; lisp/sg-saved-body-forward.lisp first.  Microcode that follows the forward
; from the leader slot meets the DTP-GC-FORWARD the file put where it leads
; and halts in ILLOP, and the case gets no answer.
;
; Preconditions: the husk static, the stack group dynamic.
(sgf-setup) => (T NIL)
; The control: the stack group resumed with its saved M-A as it left it.
(funcall *sgf-sg*) => 1
; Resumed with a body-forward in its saved M-A (SG-LOAD-BLOCK-INTO-PDL-BUFFER).
(sgf-resume) => 1
; A flip copies a stack group; its copy gets a body-forward in its saved M-A
; and is scavenged by the reclaim (SCAVL3), which keeps the word; then it is
; resumed.
(sgf-collect) => (T (DTP-BODY-FORWARD T) 1)
